(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ec-easy-2026-011"]={"v":1,"id":"ec-easy-2026-011","title":"Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC GATE Mock Test - 1","sourceTitle":"Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC GATE Mock Test - 1","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","code":"EC","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering","seriesId":"ec-easy-2026","num":11,"category":"mock","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering"},"source":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Electronics_Engineering/020_Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC GATE Mock Test - 1.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The given question is followed by three statements labelled I, II and III. You have to study the question and all the three statements given to decide whether any information provide in the statement(s) is/are redundant and can be dispensed with while answering the given question.<br />\nWhat is the average salary of 15 employees?<br />\n1. Average salary of 7 clerical cadre (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a81a9ced9a559c1fedd1.png\" /><br />\n2. Average salary of 5 officer cadre (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/542474f1352b890dc68d.png\" /><br />\n3. Average salary of the 3 sub-staff employees (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8ef1171dea637257a1dc.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b88d932d88ee84e01e4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Find the wrong number in the series:<br />\n7, 28, 63, 124, 215, 342</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7"},{"key":"B","html":"28"},{"key":"C","html":"124"},{"key":"D","html":"215"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/348dd4a978ce644b4599.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A square field ABCD of side 90 m is so located that its diagonal AC is from north to south and the corner B is to the west of D. Rohan and Rahul start walking along the sides from B and C respectively in the clockwise and anti-clockwise directions with speeds of 8 km/hr and 10 km/hr. Where shall they cross each other the second time?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"On AD at a distnace of 30 m from A."},{"key":"B","html":"On BC at a distance of 10 m from B."},{"key":"C","html":"On AD at a distance of 30 m from D."},{"key":"D","html":"On BC at a distance of 10 m from C."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e933e01cf1901775340c.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"18"},{"key":"D","html":"21"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/14e22c5fb7d36b1e2aa8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The sum of the first n terms in the sequence 7, 77, 777, 7777, .......... is _____.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8e9db928e3d46c6ab582.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/6896c04ddbd0dc215d09.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c9773669bffb7ba5bd4c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/3312653475d8b5a46df3.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b54db78fd36edddf688e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>We have two rectangular sheets of paper, M and N, each of dimensions 6 cm × 1 cm. Sheet M is rolled to form a (closed - ended) cylinder by bringing the long edges together. Sheet N is cut into equal square patches and assembled to form the largest possible closed cube. Assuming the ends of the cylinder are closed, the ratio (volume of cylinder): (Volume of cube) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b76799e079b73c4c064d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c8acf3aee7115c71d4b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cba5fc82284f27884639.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5306bb7e17c9d7bc827.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cb3d662d6f4a80a0ed8a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the adjoining figure <em>D</em>, <em>E</em> and <em>F</em> are the mid-points of the sides <em>BC</em>, <em>AC</em> and <em>AB</em> respectively.<br />\nΔ<em>DEF</em> is congruent to triangle.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/524d84853626a368beaf.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"AFE"},{"key":"B","html":"ABC"},{"key":"C","html":"BFD"},{"key":"D","html":"CDE"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa1c49da3d1f3e62c2ef.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A group of six friends named Peter, Qadir, Roger, Shah, Tarun and Usman have different height<br />\nand weight. They are ranked such that the heaviest is ranked 1 and the tallest is ranked 1 in<br />\nrespective category. Some more details are known:<br />\n<strong>I.</strong> Peter is shorter but heavier than Shah<br />\n<strong>II.</strong> Roger and Tarun are heavier but shorter than Peter and Usman<br />\n<strong>III.</strong> Shah is heavier but shorter than Qadir but neither of them is either the tallest or the heaviest.<br />\nThe rank of Qadir, if all are arranged in descending order of their height and the tallest is given rank 1, is __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e2699b69e546b9cf571.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2bd919fafa1eef1fb337.png\" /></div>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The question given below has a main statement followed by four choices. Choose the option which follows the main statement given below within the quotes.<br />\n“Whenever the demand for electricity rises, supply from GENCO increases.”</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The supply increases, it means demand has risen."},{"key":"B","html":"The demand has risen therefore the supply from GENCO increases."},{"key":"C","html":"The supply decreases implies the demand is low."},{"key":"D","html":"Both (b) and (c)"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7e88dfa13b24318adb9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Given below is a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way. Federer’s fifth grand slam win prompted a reporter to ask whether he was the best ever. Federer is certainly not lacking in confidence, but he wasn’t about to proclaim himself the best ever. “The best player of this generation, yes”, he said, “But nowhere close to ever. Just look at the records that some guys have. I’m a minnow.” _______________</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"His win against Agassi, a genius from the previous generation, contradicts that."},{"key":"B","html":"Sampras, the king of an earlier generation, was as humble."},{"key":"C","html":"He is more than a minnow to his contemporaries."},{"key":"D","html":"The difference between ‘the best of this generation’ and ‘the best ever’ is a matter of perception."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nOption &lsquo;c&rsquo; is the most appropriate way of completing the given paragraph.</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The 8-point DFT for the sequence <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d0/d0468d237aa103803f93.png\" /> The value of <em>X</em>(<em>k</em>) at <em>k</em> = 0 is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"18"},{"key":"B","html":"36"},{"key":"C","html":"48"},{"key":"D","html":"72"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/675a1fc211d121029848.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p><em>X</em>, <em>Y</em> and <em>Z</em> are three identical independent random variables, which are uniformly distributed over [0, 1]. The probability <em>P</em>(<em>X</em> ≥ <em>Y</em> ≥ <em>Z</em> ) is equal to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5ed3380e49feec97f8c6.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5ebf678b5ea1721d8d76.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/650a2e91521deaa10e4e.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/298e72237be1afaa18a0.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b0d040825a811e7e5c2a.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e376094da59dd4da43cf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The steady state error due to a unit-step disturbance input <em>D</em>(<em>s</em>) for the system shown in figure below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f02234228a77736ebd7f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1.25%"},{"key":"C","html":"2.5%"},{"key":"D","html":"∞"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/49/4906ca3548dd360c1ac1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the 4 × 1 multiplexer based circuit as shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/6586a701625e160828bb.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The combination of (<em>AB</em>), for which the output <em>Z</em> = 1, is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"01"},{"key":"B","html":"10"},{"key":"C","html":"00"},{"key":"D","html":"11"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f648f0c6e21447fecef0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The z - transform of a signal <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] = 3<sup>n</sup><em>u</em>[<em>n</em>] is X(z). The z-transform of another signal <em>y</em>[<em>n</em>] is given as, <em>Y</em>(<em>z</em>) = <em>X</em>(3z). Which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"y(1) = 1"},{"key":"B","html":"y(0) = 1"},{"key":"C","html":"y(–1) = 0"},{"key":"D","html":"y(2) = 2"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/38/384e85101a337f02bfaa.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The electron tunneling occurs in a Tunnel diode when which of the following conditions is/are satisfied?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Width of energy barrier should be narrow."},{"key":"B","html":"There should not be any empty levels present on the other side of energy barrier."},{"key":"C","html":"There should be empty levels present on the other side of energy barrier."},{"key":"D","html":"The semiconductor should be lightly doped."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)<br />\nElectron tunneling occurs in highly doped semiconductor which results in narrow width of energy barrier.<br />\nFor each tunneling carrier, there must be a filled energy state from which it can be drawn on the<br />\nsource side of the barrier and an available empty state of the same energy level to which it can go<br />\non the other side of the barrier.</p>"},{"n":17,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In an n-type gallium arsenide semiconductor at <em>T</em> = 300 K, the electron concentration varies linearly from 1 × 10<sup>18</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup> to 7 × 10<sup>17</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup> over a distance of 0.1 cm. If the material is in equilibrium, then the magnitude of diffusion current density of electrons is __________ A/cm<sup>2</sup>.<br />\n(Assume the diffusion coefficient of electrons is, <em>D<sub>n</sub></em> = 220 cm<sup>2</sup>/sec).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[104,107],"answerText":"105.6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>105.6 (104 - 107)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b09b018cd3e2208e39d6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider an n -channel MOSFET with parameters L = 1.25 μm, μ<em><sub>n</sub></em> = 650 cm<sup>2</sup>/V-s,<br />\n<em>C<sub>ox</sub></em> = 6.9 × 10<sup>–8</sup> F/cm2 and VT = 0.65 V. If the drain saturation current of the MOSFET is 4 mA for<br />\n<em>V<sub>GS</sub></em> = 5 V, then the width (<em>W</em>) of the MOSFET will be<br />\n(Assume the effect of channel length modulation is negligible)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.18 μm"},{"key":"B","html":"11.8 μm"},{"key":"C","html":"0.118 μm"},{"key":"D","html":"118 μm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/1681a618db22d914139d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The electric field of a plane wave in a lossless medium is given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91deb6a2c2a994e930fa.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>The average power density in the medium is given by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.20 W"},{"key":"B","html":"3.75 W"},{"key":"C","html":"4.25 W"},{"key":"D","html":"5.15 W"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec572bbf138c47ade839.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3bb324cc8da7e8752070.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The state space representation of a system with unity negative feedback is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/55887c57fdb80e6e2654.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The given system represents</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"an all pass system"},{"key":"B","html":"a minimum phase system"},{"key":"C","html":"a non-minimum phase system"},{"key":"D","html":"none of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/3107163f0b9980d2628c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In an experiment, positive and negative values are equally likley to occur. The probability of obtaining at most one negative value in five trials is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae52a9ec4874671e0cd4.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77982b9ccc5da14a7e43.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/182b2fb2d98bdc438092.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/0078197653a9653f3740.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ba/bae2bfcd94ab8b871743.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Let <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/862d5a52f15a835f5b0a.png\" /> If <em>I</em> is the 2 × 2 identify matrix and O is the 2 × 2 zero matrix, then</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06ce77f2cf35820acef2.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/28/2860d2ef8677a98401f0.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f5/f513196f9724774ad69c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cbedbbeab532e07bd94b.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/122696529ee61a1e00e5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The unit impulse response of a linear time invariant second order system is <em>g</em>(<em>t</em>) = 10<em>e</em><sup>–8t</sup> sin6<em>t u</em>(<em>t</em>).<br />\nThe damping ratio of the system is __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.7,0.9],"answerText":"0.80","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.80 (0.70 - 0.90)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/09096ceb29ada632f61a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the following subroutine program of an 8085 microprocessor:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9bf4cab39fc8f7b81027.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the clock frequency used in the microprocessor is 3 MHz, then the time delay produced by the given subroutine program is _______ μsec.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[97,99],"answerText":"98","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>98 (97 - 99)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5f1936968302d3b10ca.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The type of feedback topology present in the amplifier shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/42ddb6c7f6da02c802bd.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"series - shunt feedback"},{"key":"B","html":"shunt - series feedback"},{"key":"C","html":"shunt - shunt feedback"},{"key":"D","html":"series - series feedback"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nWe can see that, <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> is voltage across <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> and feedback element is <em>R</em><sub>2</sub>. Since feedback element is<br />\ndirectly connected to output node <em>V</em><sub>0</sub>, it is voltage sampling.<br />\nAlso the feedback element is connected in shunt with signal source at input. So, shunt mixing.<br />\nThus it represents voltage shunt feedback i.e. shunt - shunt feedback.</p>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A sequence <em>x</em>(<em>n</em>) with the z-transform X(z) = z<sup>4</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> – z + 1 – 2z <sup>–2</sup> is applied as an input to a linear, time-invariant system. If the impulse response of the system is h[n] = δ(1 – n) and the output is y(n), then the value of y(0) + y(1) is ___________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0,0],"answerText":"0","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0 (0 - 0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f300e7e0ed27f76691c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A BPSK signal is transmitted through an AWGN channel. The signal at channel output is received by a correlator receiver. When there is an exact phase synchronization between transmitter and receiver carrier signals, the bit error rate (BER) is Q(γ). When there is a phase error of 30° between transmitter and receiver carrier signals, the BER is Q(k γ). The value of “<em>k</em> ” is ___________. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.8,0.95],"answerText":"0.87","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.87 (0.80 - 0.95)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e02f8055b78732ecf2fc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The minimum number of flip-flops required to construct a counter, that counts from (00)<sub>16</sub> to (11)<sub>16</sub> is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,5],"answerText":"5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5 (5 - 5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/82fd42c8a79e9aa53200.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A system with impulse response, <em>h</em><sub>1</sub>[<em>n</em>] = <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01667a40399780f77ca7.png\" /> is cascaded with another system whose transfer function is, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f3650fc48a4e1569aa3e.png\" /> The overall impulse response of the cascaded system is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bbe538c9bdfec4f04b21.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/922813569f87c731d326.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac66aa89bf17d0f4261f.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f6949e147b6c57a8c329.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83b512e6b34620f6d313.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Two ‘<em>D</em>’ flip-flops are connected as a synchronous counter, that goes through the following<br />\nsequence of states (<em>Q<sub>B</sub></em> <em>Q<sub>A</sub></em>) : 00 → 01 → 10 → 11 → 00.<br />\nThe excitations for both the flip-flops should be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/972663b0aa051b89204b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd945d95a7bff6afb492.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6ce00e46896821ad6c78.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b83812b42fc3c297dc3e.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e4aaaa118f5ce21abe5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A unity negative feedback control system has an amplifier with gain <em>K</em> = 10 and gain ratio <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0f20627a5af632c371ec.png\" /> in the forward path. A derivative negative feedback H(s) = <em>K</em><sub>0</sub><em>s</em> is introduced as a minor loop around G(s). The value of derivative feedback constant <em>K</em><sub>0</sub> such that the system damping ratio is 0.6 will be _______. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.6,2],"answerText":"1.79","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.79 (1.60 - 2.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8573857faed0c40d045.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5d8e5e5ed1b0ba58b1fa.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In the circuit shown below, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/4001c30bb5d902bba9f7.png\" /></p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/047d204b104a7a0f51f1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The expression for <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74f89cbfbce2c10bbc0b.png\" /> for t > 0 is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c49665ae7844c59e5d9.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/acfda0db55ee450796f4.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/977741f58e937b9abc54.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/187177bc3bcb9c70dd1b.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/88af849a1c653eee6a39.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/27/27fbc9ec25ec46b22ac9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a series RLC circuit, instantaneous applied voltage and circuit current are given by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi></mrow></semantics></math></span></span></span><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/81b85a3d9c7a98313a13.png\" /><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nu</annotation></semantics> </math> </span></span></span> = 100sin(314t + 30°) V and <em>i</em> = 4sin (314<em>t</em> + 30°)A respectively. If inductance of the circuit is <em>L</em> = 0.25 H, then the quality factor of the circuit will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.05"},{"key":"B","html":"6.28"},{"key":"C","html":"10.02"},{"key":"D","html":"3.14"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/deaab4730f707d611dc9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the discrete memoryless channel shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0a/0a4b414300f24ed285de.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The capacity of the channel is equal to</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"zero"},{"key":"B","html":"0.5 bits/symbol"},{"key":"C","html":"0.75 bits/symbol"},{"key":"D","html":"1 bit/symbol"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/15aa447a322ca2cd1e57.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Let <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e683cba5a1f65d4cfb5b.png\" /> and <em>c</em> be the positively oriented closed curve given by <em>x</em><sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 1, z = 0. If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/444e96c7b896e1e7d93f.png\" /> then the value of a is _____.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-1,-1],"answerText":"-1","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-1</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/15bd498c834c986e2244.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In a binary baseband communication system, bit-0 and bit-1 are transmitted with probabilities 0.6 and 0.4 respectively. The received signal PDFs for both the bits are given below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/61/61f4c2d4ce6c8735b045.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Bits are decided at the output of the receiver by comparing the received signal with a threshold value. If the optimum threshold is decided using MAP criteria, then the probability of error in producing the bits at output of the receiver is equal to ________ .</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b861aee9338db9e79026.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e6c7c6c45fbdce09b12.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e1fa166c9d364ab31833.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7f23308dddd043c902ea.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/deec30129371d98ff6b8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>For a certain Bipolar junction transistor, β = 50, I<sub>CEO</sub> = 3 μA and I<sub>C</sub> = 1.2 mA. Then the value of emitter current I<sub>E</sub> is __________ mA. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1,1.4],"answerText":"1.22","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.22 (1.00 - 1.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21fb32043160b174fa9d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In circuit shown, opamps are ideal. The frequency and preak-to-peak values of output are</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/3992d1baa4857729ec0c.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10 kHz, 24 V"},{"key":"B","html":"2.5 kHz, 12 V"},{"key":"C","html":"7.5 kHz, 24 V"},{"key":"D","html":"5 kHz, 12 V"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/36/36e1dd8e8f8a34f18f63.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In the given circuit, diodes <em>D</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>D</em><sub>2</sub> are ideal. If <em>C</em><sub>1</sub> = 5 pF and <em>C</em><sub>2</sub> = 10 pF, then the values of <em>V</em><sub><em>C</em>1 </sub>and <em>V</em><sub><em>C</em>2</sub> respectively at steady state will be</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f37ffae97be287ed17b.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0 V and 15 V"},{"key":"B","html":"15 V and 15 V"},{"key":"C","html":"0 V and 0 V"},{"key":"D","html":"15 V and 0 V"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3a/3a8f4c858aae469f8a91.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In the circuit given below, all diodes are ideal.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e6a9b9c4bb0049a995c4.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The value of output voltage <em>V</em><sub>out</sub> is equal to _______ V.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/27/27d661b7c5a35685dc26.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92f585f9e2c54bfdc105.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/090b8dca12b1c3d5b610.png\" /> = 0.7 V and β = 100 for both the transistors, then the value of output voltage <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> will be _________ V. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,4.5],"answerText":"3.91","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.91 (3.00 - 4.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f4/f447557633636c08f21a.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0eff55cc3588bb62e5ad.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The open loop transfer function of a unity negative feedback control system is given by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/42ec02112c65b7863ba7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The phase margin of the system is ________ (in degrees) (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[16,18.5],"answerText":"17.96","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>17.96 (16.00 - 18.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53c6efef0f79c20cf658.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A 100 Ω lossless transmission line is terminated by a load of (150 + j100)Ω. If the line is excited by a 100 MHz source, then the ratio of voltage maximum to voltage minimum on the line is ___________. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.35,2.5],"answerText":"2.42","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.42 (2.35 - 2.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f88bf1d54759366cb7cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider a unity feedback system with forward path gain</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d024bd65a4633b738fc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the system is producing undamped oscillations with the frequency of 2 rad/sec, then the value of <em>K</em> is equal to ________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1,1],"answerText":"1","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a8c904f6bf69e348fd0a.png\" /></div>\n\n<p>(1 - 1)</p>"},{"n":45,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An audio signal bandlimited to 15 kHz is sampled with Nyquist rate and quantized with a 512- level uniform quantizer. The resultant bits are baseband modelled using a raised cosine filter with roll-off factor of 0.25. The minimum channel bandwidth required to transmit this baseband modelled signal is equal to _______ kHz. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[167,170],"answerText":"168.75","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>168.75 (167.00 - 170.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9a6146a51137e6dddec9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The logic circuit, that corresponds to the state transition diagram shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/69fd2e3a427fa57e74c8.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>J</em> - <em>K</em> flip flop"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>R</em> - <em>S</em> flip flop"},{"key":"C","html":"MOD-2 counter"},{"key":"D","html":"NAND gate"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19c08b60135c62b307dd.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85c787d82be5220aa134.png\" /> with y(0) = 1, then y(3) = ____.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.03,0.05],"answerText":"0.04","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.04 (0.03 - 0.05)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/698179fa17d190a841d1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d23b290813b3df99869.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"sin(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"B","html":"–sin(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"C","html":"cos(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"D","html":"tan(2<em>u</em>)"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/30db453539f5791644da.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For an FM radio receiver, <em>f<sub>c</sub></em> is the received carrier frequency, <em>f</em><sub>LO</sub> is the local oscillator frequency and <em>f</em><sub>IF</sub> is the intermediate frequency. The receiver is designed to receive the signals in the range (88 to 108) MHz. If <em>f</em><sub>LO</sub> is always less than fc, then the minimum value of <em>f</em><sub>IF</sub> required to avoid the problem of image frequency is __________ MHz.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9.9,10.1],"answerText":"10","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>10 (9.90 - 10.10)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae20cf76f7b6619aa130.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A resistance <em>R</em> and an initially relaxed capacitor of 5 μF are connected in series across a 100 V d.c. supply. If the voltage across the capacitor becomes 50 V in 5 sec after the circuit is switched on, then the corresponding value of <em>R</em> is ________ MΩ. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.2,1.6],"answerText":"1.44","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.44 (1.20 - 1.60)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7c1a1c0a2fac0f74f5c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In circuit shown, all MOSFETs are identical and they are biased to operate in saturation region. If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc615a94ae03855f41ed.png\" />then <em>V</em><sub>out</sub> is _________. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ee/eebbabfd1ec838fbef0b.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5.2,5.4],"answerText":"5.33","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5.33 (5.20 - 5.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e6d7688cf0d8e71df45f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An ideal MOS capacitor with p-type substrate has an oxide layer with thickness of 1.8 μm and the ratio ε<em><sub>si</sub></em> / ε<em><sub>ox</sub></em> = 3. Due to the application of gate voltage, a surface potential of 0.035 V has been developed at the semiconductor-oxide layer interface, and a depletion region of width 0.4 μm is created inside the semiconductor. The gate voltage applied is ___________ V. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.9,1.1],"answerText":"0.98","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.98 (0.90 - 1.10)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/48b60c161478e8d0e7e4.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b2dd4771640ef56d957.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A 3 cm × 2 cm rectangular waveguide is filled with a lossless dielectric material (ε<sub>r</sub> = 4). If the waveguide is operating in TE<sub>11</sub> mode at 20 GHz, the phase velocity is __________ × 10<sup>8</sup> m/s.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.45,1.65],"answerText":"1.54","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.54 (1.45 - 1.65)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f43925be73e16e156f0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the network shown below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c651e49f4f4bba75520.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The maximum power that can be transferred to the load <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3.125 W"},{"key":"B","html":"4.625 W"},{"key":"C","html":"5.525 W"},{"key":"D","html":"6.250 W"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/4768753d35cbe2940858.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>It is required to interface a 4K × 8 memory chip to an 8085 microprocessor. If the starting address assigned to the memory chip is CE00H, then the address of the last memory location of the memory chip (in decimal) is __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[56831,56831],"answerText":"56831","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>56831 (56831 - 56831)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e21c99664e450cfc07d7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A plane wave propagating in free space with magnetic field component,</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a8222dd962aa72902d87.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>is incident normally on a lossless medium (ε<sub>r</sub> = 2, μ<sub>r</sub> = 8) in region <em>x</em> ≥ 0. The reflected electric field vector is given by</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8b925c7273ba3d7aa29a.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/00f1825c44663908c4a8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/6094f6d2ae522d3bdc8e.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/35ddd69d4e42fbc85d44.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d7236313947917e54af.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider an <em>npn</em> bipolar junction transistor. Assume that diffusion constant and diffusion length in emitter and base regions are same. Then the ratio of emitter doping to base doping in order to achieve an emitter injection efficiency of 0.9967 is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"202"},{"key":"B","html":"302"},{"key":"C","html":"352"},{"key":"D","html":"412"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/17c0ff5f53a27cedd04e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the function <em>f</em>(<em>t</em>) whose Laplace transform is,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae17766e7574d2d35c11.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If <em>e</em><sup>1.5t</sup> <em>f</em>(<em>t</em>) is stable, then the function <em>f</em>(<em>t</em>) is given by</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/636c7e016fe4bef82d82.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a13ac20b5272bbbde659.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/df8c52515a9bf9173d18.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c82aa1c686d51046c3ce.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e83c056a3558e73bc660.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An LTI system has transfer function, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b412bfd958772fb1eaf.png\" /> Which of the given options is/are correct regarding the above system?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/404df9a2bae230f438c0.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b968291d1254d7a5716e.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"The given LTI system is both stable and causal."},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92ae26343b459c8b3e97.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/429a725655fd7b788472.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b6eafee3d90d3f6a8ac.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An EM wave is incident on a slab of conducting material whose slab width is thinner than its skin depth. Which of the following will not happen?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Part of incident wave will be reflected, none of it will be transmitted, and part of it will be trapped inside the slab."},{"key":"B","html":"All of the incident wave will be reflected off the slab and there will be no transmitted wave."},{"key":"C","html":"All of the incident wave’s energy will be absorbed by the slab so that there is no reflected wave and no transmitted wave."},{"key":"D","html":"A significant portion of the incident wave’s energy will pass through the conducting slab and generate a transmitted wave on the other side."}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)<br />\nSince the slab thickness is less than the skin depth, a significant portion of the EM wave&rsquo;s energy<br />\nis passed on the other side without being heavily attenuated. Hence, options (a), (b) and (c) are not correct.</p>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the following operational amplifier circuit, <em>R<sub>f</sub></em> = 8 kΩ and <em>R</em><sub>in</sub> = 2 kΩ. Which of the following statements about the given circuit is/are correct?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99098c0410de5be8dd41.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"For |<em>V</em><sub>in</sub>| > 2.5 V, Op-amp is in saturation region."},{"key":"B","html":"For |<em>V</em><sub>in</sub>| > 2.5 V, Op-amp is in linear region."},{"key":"C","html":"For |<em>V</em><sub>in</sub>| ≤ 2.5 V, Op-amp is in linear region."},{"key":"D","html":"For |<em>V</em><sub>in</sub>| ≤ 2.5 V, Op-amp is in saturation region."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8b518b32e283b488a630.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The Brewster angle for a parallel polarized wave traveling from air into teflon for which ε<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 2.1 is _______ degrees. (upto one decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[55,56],"answerText":"55.4","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>55.4 (55.0 - 56.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c6181a523c7ea5c95ab8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The daily consumption of electric power (in millions of kW-hours) is a Random variable having the <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c7338d624a8efbc785d6.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>If the total production is 12 million kW-hours, the probability that there is power cut (shortage) on any given day is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"4 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"5 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"6 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/57/571f6b3115f10e26ff4f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The determinant of the given matrix is ____________.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d315b8c8a3e600750565.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[12,12],"answerText":"12","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>12</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/49/4915769bbdf4060e4d11.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the function of complex variable:</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff6cc2eedfd09b2efc89.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The sum of singularities of f(z) is _____.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,5],"answerText":"5","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/61/612c331e7ad880be6e07.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":33,"MSQ":6,"NAT":26},"withoutKey":0}};
